    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Bryce Harper**, who stands as our clear anchor with an elite 80.21 score against Bieber. The favorable matchup against an xERA of 5.23, combined with a spot in the three-hole and positive park factors, makes **Bryce Harper** an automatic start. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an essential piece today; despite a neutral park environment, his ability to capitalize on the platoon advantage and his high-leverage spot in the order result in a strong 67.98 rating. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against V\u00e1squez, with **Daulton Varsho** (67.31) and **Yainer Diaz** (60.47) both projected for significant output. **Justin Crawford** also warrants a strong endorsement; while his #9 spot in the order suppresses his floor, his elite profile against a weak starter like Bieber makes him a high-upside play to chase stolen bases, our scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Kyle Karros**, who posted a respectable 49.55 score but ultimately lost out to the superior platoon efficiencies of our starting core. While **Kyle Karros** holds value, the optimizer prioritized the high-ceiling matchups afforded to **Dylan Beavers** (59.49) and **Gavin Sheets** (58.97), both of whom benefit from favorable SP skill metrics today. Risks remain, particularly with **Yainer Diaz** and **Daulton Varsho**, as both are currently waiting on finalized lineups; should they shift lower in the batting order, their efficiency scores will likely see a downward adjustment. We are also keeping a watchful eye on **Cal Raleigh**, whose score of 47.71 is buoyed by a platoon edge but suppressed by a tough outing against Seymour, serving as a reminder that we must monitor these games closely to preserve our season-long innings and game caps.",
